  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 117 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThe Heat Advisory has been extended in time to include Saturday\nand ends at 8 PM that evening. Though, it is likely that the\nAdvisory gets extended through Labor Day Weekend due to the\nlongevity of the heat and warm overnight temperatures in the\n70s. This heat isn't expected to end anytime soon. The reason\nwhy we haven't upgraded to an Extreme Heat Warning is because of\nthe uncertainty in daily heat index values. Guidance is hinting\nat a drier air mass moving into the area for the weekend which\nwould impact our heat index values. The past few afternoons have\ntrended drier than model guidance with the exception of today\ndue to the small bit of moisture that has moved into the area.\nWith that in mind, this may keep our heat index values below\nExtreme Heat Warning criteria (HI of 110 degrees). Though, it \nwon't change the fact of it'll still feel hot if you're \nparticipating in any outdoor activities this weekend. Remember\nthe rest of the week into the weekend will feature a Major to\nExtreme HeatRisk across our area. Be sure to hydrate and take\nbreaks from the heat this weekend, especially with no overnight\nrelief. \n\nVery low-end POPs of 15-30% move into the area on Sunday as a \nweak front is forecast to move through. However, temperatures\nwon't change much to start next week with highs still in the\n90s.",
